<title>USA: Halliburton says in talks to buy OGC.</title>
<headline>Halliburton says in talks to buy OGC.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Halliburton Co on Monday confirmed it is in talks to buy OGC International Plc. It gave no details.</p>
<p>Earlier today, OGS said it London it had received an approach from Halliburton that might lead to an offer for OGC.</p>
<p>OGC provides engineering and other operations to the petroleum industry, mostly in the North Sea. The company had revenues of $385 million and pre-tax profit of $23.5 million in 1995, Halliburton said.</p>
<p>For the first six months of 1996, OGC had revenues of $150 million and pre-tax profit of $4.5 million, Halliburton added.</p>
